CORE
main.c
--pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 22 .*pointer NULL in \*p: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 22 .*pointer NULL in \*p: SUCCESS$
--
At a control-flow merge a pointer may have been reassigned differently on each
incoming path (here NULL on one, a valid object on the other). Cached
pointer-validity assertions established on one path must be cleared at the
merge. Without that, the dereference at line 22 is deduplicated against the
cached check from the else branch and the NULL path is never asserted.
